      "writtenOn": "2021-11-24T19:48:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`BAZEL_METRICS_DIR` is `out/bazel_metrics` at the point of me writing out \"bp2build_metrics.pb\". Because that dir doesn\u0027t exist (anywhere under `out/`), I can\u0027t output to it (and am unsure whether it\u0027s OK for me to just mkdir). Should I push forward some e.g. logging directory from higher in the call chain? If so, should I introduce a new env var?",
      "parentUuid": "a86a22d0_f3f2105d",
      "revId": "6948f2d22a5fe1467d87e5d6fc47165f41991186",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ded9b300_4bf195c0",
        "filename": "cmd/soong_build/main.go",
        "patchSetId": 29
      },
      "lineNbr": 538,
      "author": {
        "id": 1605027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-24T20:42:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I think it would be good to identify the appropriate logs directory in soong_ui, forward this to soong_build via a new environment variable (as is done for BAZEL_METRICS_DIR, but do it with a brand new env variable). I don\u0027t think you can re-use BAZEL_METRICS_DIR here.\n\nThough, brainstormin:\nConsider that we might set a new environment variable LOG_DIR to the value of `c.LogsDir()` in soong_ui. soong_build will then read LOG_DIR from the environment to get the appropriate logs directory. It can then determine the bazel metrics directory using `${LOG_DIR}/bazel_metrics` -- it need not obtain it from BAZEL_METRICS_DIR, thus we may not need BAZEL_METRICS_DIR at all.\n\nThat refactoring (the removal of BAZEL_METRICS_DIR) is probably best suited for a followup CL, though, if we choose to go that way.",
      "parentUuid": "119602b2_765d2716",
      "revId": "6948f2d22a5fe1467d87e5d6fc47165f41991186",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
